{"parentUuid":"a87005e3-664e-4c9d-9a80-c85a3a7e4ee9","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a3dd1dc86014a90af","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011MV9pLeCPEXsgVtXraNF74","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Wm1Ht5J5WzmJtSzMpKuD8Y","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"GNN 2D rectangle packing facility placement layout optimization combinatorial"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8005,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"output_tokens":324,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8005},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":324,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8005,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8005,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaooxJLcqkaDWD8r1ddba","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"0d8ffe9d-1e33-4e5c-b90f-cd4e998ff901","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:14.673Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c7934360-f7b9-4d96-a683-ab8882b5099b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a3dd1dc86014a90af","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JxyJs2m8aQSqFCKQPPVsoN","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"NeuroSAT scaling large SAT instances 2024 GNN variable branching\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Learning to Rank the Initial Branching Order of SAT Solvers\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2603.07176v1\"},{\"title\":\"Improving CDCL SAT Solving using Graph Neural Networks\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2110.14053\"},{\"title\":\"Published as a conference paper at ICLR 2024\",\"url\":\"https://export.arxiv.org/pdf/2110.14053\"},{\"title\":\"1 Introduction\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2504.01173\"},{\"title\":\"SAT-GATv2: A Dynamic Attention-Based Graph Neural Network for Solving Boolean Satisfiability Problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2079-9292/14/3/423\"},{\"title\":\"NEUROBACK: IMPROVING CDCL SAT SOLVING USING ...\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=samyfu6G93\"},{\"title\":\"Neural Approaches to SAT Solving: Design Choices and Interpretability\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2504.01173\"},{\"title\":\"Combining Graph Neural Networks with Expert Knowledge ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2405.11024\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] Learning a SAT Solver from Single-Bit Supervision | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Learning-a-SAT-Solver-from-Single-Bit-Supervision-Selsam-Lamm/fe257027193ea4a74fdab99d7509ce4002ad7de6\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - zhaoyu-li/G4SATBench: [TMLR 2024] G4SATBench: Benchmarking and Advancing SAT Solving with Graph Neural Networks\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/zhaoyu-li/G4SATBench\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about NeuroSAT, scaling large SAT instances, GNNs, and variable branching:\n\n## Overview of NeuroSAT\n\nNeuroSAT was the first framework adapting a neural model into an end-to-end SAT solver, which was not intended as a complete SAT solver. The NeuroSAT architecture is derived from a GNN framework for SAT solving, with the main advantage that it is recurrent and therefore the number of message passing iterations is theoretically not limited.\n\n## Scaling Challenges\n\nWhen it comes to scaling to large SAT instances, approaches aiming to provide SAT solvers with better branching or phase selection heuristics either reduce the number of solving iterations or enhance the solving effectiveness on selected small-scale problems with up to a few thousand variables, but they do not provide obvious improvements in solving effectiveness for large-scale problems. Additionally, NeuroSAT's scalability declines notably on larger and more complex problem instances.\n\n## Recent Advances in Variable Branching\n\nA GNN pipeline can predict branching order with speed-ups over multiple domains, and often generalizes to instances that are up to an order of magnitude larger than instances given during training. This represents recent work (from 2024-2026) that addresses variable branching order prediction specifically.\n\nFor more practical improvements on large-scale problems, NeuroCore aims to make the solving more effective especially for large-scale problems as in SAT competitions.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5f3bb7e3-aec1-4272-9505-427686893fc1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:19.811Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c7934360-f7b9-4d96-a683-ab8882b5099b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8195bca9-6036-48b4-8d2b-37f43db19333","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a3dd1dc86014a90af","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UXRXythcA26J63L7hmJz2s","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"learning to branch CP-SAT Gurobi GNN imitation strong branching 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Boolean Satisfiability via Imitation Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2509.25411\"},{\"title\":\"Learning to Branch in Combinatorial Optimization With Graph Pointer Networks\",\"url\":\"https://www.ieee-jas.net/article/doi/10.1109/JAS.2023.124113\"},{\"title\":\"Towards Imitation Learning to Branch for MIP: A Hybrid Reinforcement Learning based Sample Augmentation Approach | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=NdcQQ82mfy\"},{\"title\":\"Learning to Rank the Initial Branching Order of SAT Solvers\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2603.07176v1\"},{\"title\":\"Lookback for Learning to Branch\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=EQpGkw5rvL\"},{\"title\":\"Machine learning augmented branch and bound for mixed integer linear programming | Mathematical Programming | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10107-024-02130-y\"},{\"title\":\"Published as a conference paper at ICLR 2025 LEARNING TO SELECT NODES IN BRANCH\",\"url\":\"https://proceedings.iclr.cc/paper_files/paper/2025/file/82f625a28d822d2748b9f5c4f9a89bb9-Paper-Conference.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"TOWARDS IMITATION LEARNING TO BRANCH FOR MIP\",\"url\":\"https://proceedings.iclr.cc/paper_files/paper/2024/file/850cc7c4e5619fdc2f30c4eaa5ce3c17-Paper-Conference.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Learning to Compare Nodes in Branch and Bound with Graph Neural Networks\",\"url\":\"https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2022/file/cf5bb18807a3e9cfaaa51e667e18f807-Paper-Conference.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SORREL: Suboptimal-Demonstration-Guided\",\"url\":\"https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/AAAI/article/download/33219/35374\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for your query. Here's a summary of the relevant research findings:\n\n## Key Research Areas\n\nThe search results reveal several recent developments in learning to branch for combinatorial optimization solvers:\n\n**Recent 2024-2025 Work:**\n\nRecent research casts branching as a sequential modeling problem by collapsing solver runs into compact sequences of surviving decisions, which serve as clean, conflict-free training targets aligned with prefix-conditioned autoregressive modeling.\n\nRecent integrations of learning inside solvers include NeuroSelect (2024) for clause deletion policies, NeuroBack (2024) for phase initialization with GNNs, and RDC-SAT (2025) adopting a divide-and-conquer strategy via reinforcement learning.\n\n**Imitation Learning and Strong Branching:**\n\nGNNs are trained offline on MILP instances to imitate strong branching, a very good but computationally expensive branching heuristic.\n\nA graph pointer network model has been proposed to learn branch rules, trained to imitate the expert strong branching rule by a tailored top-k Kullback-Leibler divergence loss function.\n\n**Gurobi and Solver Comparisons:**\n\nSome learning-based models excel in making superior branching decisions compared to state-of-the-art learning-based models and the open-source solver SCIP, notably often outperforming Gurobi.\n\nGurobi is a state-of-the-art commercial solver with hybrid expert branching rules which is known often much more effective than open-source solvers.\n\n**Recent Advances (2024):**\n\nHybrid approaches combining online and offline reinforcement learning techniques have been proposed to enhance training samples for branching policy learning.\n\nThe search results include recent papers from ICLR 2024-2025 conferences and arXiv submissions from early 2026, demonstrating active ongoing research in this field.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e32724a7-f46f-4133-9912-2c01f1ea41f1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:22.003Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8195bca9-6036-48b4-8d2b-37f43db19333","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0d8ffe9d-1e33-4e5c-b90f-cd4e998ff901","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a3dd1dc86014a90af","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wm1Ht5J5WzmJtSzMpKuD8Y","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"GNN 2D rectangle packing facility placement layout optimization combinatorial\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A multi-population genetic algorithm for a constrained two-dimensional orthogonal packing problem – Optimization Online\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/2009/01/2187/\"},{\"title\":\"A new metaheuristic genetic-based placement algorithm for 2D strip packing | Journal of Industrial Engineering International\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s40092-014-0047-9\"},{\"title\":\"Optimizing 2D irregular packing via image processing and computational intelligence | Scientific Reports\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-025-97202-0\"},{\"title\":\"Optimal Rectangle Packing: Initial Results\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/2933135_Optimal_Rectangle_Packing_Initial_Results\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Optimal Rectangle Packing: An Absolute Placement Approach\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/260039071_Optimal_Rectangle_Packing_An_Absolute_Placement_Approach\"},{\"title\":\"A Simple Solution for Shape Packing in 2D\",\"url\":\"https://www.gorillasun.de/blog/a-simple-solution-for-shape-packing-in-2d/\"},{\"title\":\"Hierarchical Rectangle Packing Solved by Multi-Level Recursive Logic-based Benders Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2512.20239\"},{\"title\":\"Online calculator: 2D Bin Packing Problem Solver\",\"url\":\"https://planetcalc.com/8634/\"},{\"title\":\"GFPack++: Improving 2D Irregular Packing by Learning Gradient Field with Attention\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2406.07579v1\"},{\"title\":\"Optimizing 2D+1 Packing in Constrained Environments Using Deep Reinforcement Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2503.17573v1\"}]\n\nI've performed the web search for your query on GNN-based 2D rectangle packing for facility placement, layout optimization, and combinatorial problems. Here's a summary of the key findings:\n\n## Overview of 2D Rectangle Packing and Layout Optimization\n\nThe 2D strip packing problem is a complex NP-hard combinatorial optimization problem that has multiple applications including facility layout design.\n\n## Key Research Areas\n\n**Traditional and Hybrid Approaches:**\nThe constrained two-dimensional (2D), non-guillotine restricted packing problem uses approaches that hybridize novel placement procedures with genetic algorithms based on random keys.\n\n**Facility Layout Applications:**\nThe facility layout problem is an application in which packing is used to design efficient factory or office layouts with respect to the flow of people and material, with a two-level hierarchy of packing sub-problems.\n\n**Deep Learning Approaches:**\nIn GFPack, a graph network determined by the distances between polygons is employed to facilitate state encoding, however this approach overlooks the geometric relationships among the polygons. More recent work like GFPack++ utilizes attention-based learning of gradient fields and supports continuous rotation, substantially improving generalization capabilities.\n\n**Reinforcement Learning Methods:**\nA novel approach based on deep reinforcement learning (DRL) for the 2D+1 packing problem with spatial constraints extends the traditional 2D packing problem, incorporating an additional constraint on the height dimension.\n\nThe research shows an evolution from genetic algorithms and heuristic methods toward neural network-based and machine learning approaches for solving these combinatorial optimization problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"013f11f8-c37e-4bb1-9e77-b3bb888322d4","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:22.258Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0d8ffe9d-1e33-4e5c-b90f-cd4e998ff901","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a87005e3-664e-4c9d-9a80-c85a3a7e4ee9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a3dd1dc86014a90af","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012ziZgfLV4dTnFXtcaAhAof","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"DeepMind Neural MIP solver 2024 graph neural network branch and bound\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"[2012.13349] Solving Mixed Integer Programs Using Neural Networks\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.13349\"},{\"title\":\"DeepMind & Google Use Neural Networks to Solve Mixed Integer Programs | Synced\",\"url\":\"https://syncedreview.com/2021/08/03/deepmind-podracer-tpu-based-rl-frameworks-deliver-exceptional-performance-at-low-cost-74/\"},{\"title\":\"DeepMind & Google Use Neural Networks to Solve Mixed Integer Programs | by Synced | SyncedReview | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/syncedreview/deepmind-google-use-neural-networks-to-solve-mixed-integer-programs-bf41e3521950\"},{\"title\":\"Solving Mixed Integer Programs Using Neural Networks | DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.com/research/publications/2021/Solving-Mixed-Integer-Programs-Using-Neural-Networks\"},{\"title\":\"Solving Mixed Integer Programs Using Neural Networks\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2012.13349\"},{\"title\":\"MIP-GNN: A Data-Driven Framework for Guiding Combinatorial Solvers | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/361741429_MIP-GNN_A_Data-Driven_Framework_for_Guiding_Combinatorial_Solvers\"},{\"title\":\"Deep learning enhanced mixed integer optimization: Learning to reduce model dimensionality - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0098135424001431\"},{\"title\":\"Solving Mixed Integer Programs Using Neural Networks\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/347880794_Solving_Mixed_Integer_Programs_Using_Neural_Networks\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] Solving Mixed Integer Programs Using Neural Networks | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Solving-Mixed-Integer-Programs-Using-Neural-Nair-Bartunov/81d304d20a7b8a21006ddf39dfb09627b9ff1a5f\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co: Awesome machine learning for combinatorial optimization papers. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about DeepMind's neural network approach to Mixed Integer Programming (MIP) solving, though the work appears to be from 2020-2021 rather than 2024:\n\n## DeepMind Neural MIP Solver Overview\n\nA team from DeepMind and Google Research leverages neural networks to automatically construct effective heuristics from a dataset for mixed integer programming (MIP) problems. \n\nThe approach consists of two main neural network-based components:\n\n1. **Neural Diving**: Neural Diving learns a deep neural network to generate multiple partial assignments for its integer variables, and the resulting smaller MIPs for un-assigned variables are solved with SCIP to construct high quality joint assignments.\n\n2. **Neural Branching**: Neural Branching learns a deep neural network to make variable selection decisions in branch-and-bound to bound the objective value gap with a small tree. This is done by imitating a new variant of Full Strong Branching we propose that scales to large instances using GPUs.\n\n## Performance Results\n\nComparing solvers with respect to primal-dual gap averaged over a held-out set of instances, the learning-augmented SCIP is 2× to 10× better on all datasets except one on which it is 10^5× better, at large time limits. The approach was evaluated on six diverse real-world datasets, including two Google production datasets and MIPLIB, by training separate neural networks on each. Most instances in all the datasets combined have 10^3-10^6 variables and constraints after presolve, which is significantly larger than previous learning approaches.\n\nNote: While the search returned results primarily from 2020-2021, there is also mention of more recent 2024 work on GNN-based approaches for MIP solving in the search results, though specific details about a 2024 release weren't prominently featured.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ba6f8c73-5a47-4b01-96ec-46266a435f53","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:22.839Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a87005e3-664e-4c9d-9a80-c85a3a7e4ee9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
