{"parentUuid":"e7c10bab-6210-4b22-b713-2b605d174e20","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a3dd1dc86014a90af","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01277HSkga9esfM5WT6TZMdm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DPKbhbGEb9cvB1Li8PngzJ","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"CP-SAT hint warm start solution OR-Tools machine learning initial solution 2024"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1327,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4612,"cache_read_input_tokens":21118,"output_tokens":328,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4612},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1327,"output_tokens":328,"cache_read_input_tokens":21118,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4612,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4612,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaooyRR3oB7DAVWtCr9jV","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"b9d72e84-d666-4818-a800-abd2efe26dfb","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:28.707Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"4c1a20a3-e83c-425c-a70e-3d156efd6dcd","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a3dd1dc86014a90af","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LpEqJGFpciumN5nEC53f2g","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Khalil learning to branch GCN Gasse 2019 ecole exact imitation strong branching benchmark\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Learning in Spatial Branching: Limitations of Strong Branching Imitation\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2406.03626v1\"},{\"title\":\"IMPROVING LEARNING TO BRANCH VIA ...\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=M_KwRsbhi5e\"},{\"title\":\"Learning to Branch in Combinatorial Optimization with ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2307.01434\"},{\"title\":\"Lookback for Learning to Branch\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=EQpGkw5rvL\"},{\"title\":\"Learning to Branch in Mixed Integer Programming | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/361562127_Learning_to_Branch_in_Mixed_Integer_Programming\"},{\"title\":\"Learning to branch with Tree-aware Branching Transformers - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0950705122007298\"},{\"title\":\"Reinforcement Learning for Branch-and-Bound Optimisation\",\"url\":\"https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/AAAI/article/view/25521/25293\"},{\"title\":\"ecole/examples/branching-imitation/example.ipynb at master · ds4dm/ecole\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ds4dm/ecole/blob/master/examples/branching-imitation/example.ipynb\"},{\"title\":\"YORDLE: An Efficient Imitation Learning for Branch and Bound Qingyu Qu\",\"url\":\"https://www.ecole.ai/2021/ml4co-competition/proceedings/7.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Learning in Spatial Branching: Limitations of Strong Branching Imitation\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/381227571_Learning_in_Spatial_Branching_Limitations_of_Strong_Branching_Imitation\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about the research you're asking about. Gasse et al. (2019) published \"Exact combinatorial optimization with graph convolutional neural networks\" in Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems.\n\nThis work is a significant contribution to machine learning for combinatorial optimization. Gasse et al. developed a novel GCN model for learning the variable selection strategy, exploiting the variable-constraint bipartite graph feature of mixed-integer linear programs (MIPs), and trained the model to mimic the strong branching policy by imitation learning.\n\nThe research is also associated with Ecole (Extensible Combinatorial Optimization Learning Environments) library along with PySCIPOpt and SCIP 7.0.1 as the backend solver. This work was part of a broader literature focused on learning to imitate strong branching, as in Khalil et al. (2016), Alvarez et al. (2017), Balcan et al. (2018), Gasse et al. (2019), and Gupta et al. (2020).\n\nThe Gasse et al. 2019 work represents a key advance in using graph neural networks for learning branching decisions in exact combinatorial optimization.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"61bc74ce-b0c0-45e5-a059-79781e4e02d4","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:32.437Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4c1a20a3-e83c-425c-a70e-3d156efd6dcd","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"bfb47999-2e3f-4a5f-8dc9-e104ce3565e5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a3dd1dc86014a90af","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WMGJAcyZNW57MsyqCvhkXd","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Mirhoseini chip placement reinforcement learning Google 2021 graph neural network VLSI\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Chip Design with Deep Reinforcement Learning\",\"url\":\"https://research.google/blog/chip-design-with-deep-reinforcement-learning/\"},{\"title\":\"[2004.10746] Chip Placement with Deep Reinforcement Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.10746\"},{\"title\":\"A graph placement methodology for fast chip design | Nature\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-021-03544-w\"},{\"title\":\"A graph placement methodology for fast chip design | Scaling Intelligence Lab at Stanford University\",\"url\":\"https://scalingintelligence.stanford.edu/pubs/gpm/\"},{\"title\":\"A graph placement methodology for fast chip design - PubMed\",\"url\":\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34108699/\"},{\"title\":\"Mirhoseini Et Al. - 2021 - A Graph Placement Methodology For Fast Chip Design | PDF | Computer Engineering\",\"url\":\"https://www.scribd.com/document/838297340/Mirhoseini-et-al-2021-A-graph-placement-methodology-for-fast-chip-design\"},{\"title\":\"A graph placement methodology for fast chip design\",\"url\":\"https://gwern.net/doc/reinforcement-learning/model/2021-mirhoseini.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] A graph placement methodology for fast chip design | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/A-graph-placement-methodology-for-fast-chip-design-Mirhoseini-Goldie/07aa07cb6791f336cb32643d54201eab295b2757\"},{\"title\":\"A graph placement methodology for fast chip design\",\"url\":\"https://www.cl.cam.ac.uk/~ey204/teaching/ACS/R244_2021_2022/papers/Mirhoseini_NATURE_2021.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Chip Design with Deep Reinforcement Learning – Google Research Blog\",\"url\":\"https://ai.googleblog.com/2020/04/chip-design-with-deep-reinforcement.html?m=1\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Azalia Mirhoseini's work on chip placement using reinforcement learning and graph neural networks:\n\n## Overview\n\nThe research presents a deep reinforcement learning approach to chip floorplanning that automatically generates chip floorplans superior or comparable to those produced by humans in all key metrics (power consumption, performance, and chip area), using an edge-based graph convolutional neural network architecture capable of learning rich and transferable representations of the chip.\n\n## Key Technical Approach\n\nThe netlist graph and the current node are passed through an edge-based graph neural network to encode the input state. The policy network generates a probability distribution over all possible grid cells onto which the current node could be placed. RL training is guided by a fast-but-approximate reward signal calculated using the weighted average of approximate wirelength and approximate congestion.\n\n## Performance and Impact\n\nThe method automatically generates chip floorplans in under six hours that are superior or comparable to those produced by humans in all key metrics, including power consumption, performance and chip area. The method was used to design the next generation of Google's artificial intelligence accelerators.\n\n## Publication Timeline\n\nIn June 2021, methods were published in Nature that have been used in production to design the next generation of Google TPUs.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e513b847-c962-4e40-b864-9489c2e1e5ac","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:33.367Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bfb47999-2e3f-4a5f-8dc9-e104ce3565e5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e7c10bab-6210-4b22-b713-2b605d174e20","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a3dd1dc86014a90af","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014F3yhHVHi4aqhyUXYXFYTb","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CombOptNet learning combinatorial optimization integer programming end-to-end pretrained model\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CombOptNet: Fit the Right NP-Hard Problem by Learning ...\",\"url\":\"http://proceedings.mlr.press/v139/paulus21a/paulus21a.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - mathworks/Neural-Combinatorial-Optimization-with-Pointer-Network: Combinatorial Optimization (CO) seeks the best solution from a finite, but often exponentially large, set of possibilities. Traditional solvers can face computational challenges on large instances. Neural combinatorial optimization (NCO) is using a different approach to solve such problems, by learning heuristics or policies using neural networks. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mathworks/Neural-Combinatorial-Optimization-with-Pointer-Network\"},{\"title\":\"[2105.02343] CombOptNet: Fit the Right NP-Hard Problem by Learning Integer Programming Constraints\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2105.02343\"},{\"title\":\"CombOptNet: Fit the Right NP-Hard Problem by Learning Integer Programming Constraints\",\"url\":\"https://papertalk.org/papertalks/32350\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - martius-lab/CombOptNet: Source code for the Paper: CombOptNet: Fit the Right NP-Hard Problem by Learning Integer Programming Constraints}\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/martius-lab/CombOptNet\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] CombOptNet: Fit the Right NP-Hard Problem by Learning Integer Programming Constraints | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/CombOptNet:-Fit-the-Right-NP-Hard-Problem-by-Paulus-Rol'inek/1695324c0f5233a5b62fa52f12ae2d2e8bf22fa8\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) CombOptNet: Fit the Right NP-Hard Problem by Learning Integer Programming Constraints\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/351369325_CombOptNet_Fit_the_Right_NP-Hard_Problem_by_Learning_Integer_Programming_Constraints\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co: Awesome machine learning for combinatorial optimization papers. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co\"},{\"title\":\"CombOptNet: Fit the Right NP-Hard Problem by Learning Integer Programming\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/media/icml-2021/Slides/9555.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Fit The Right NP-Hard Problem: End-to-end Learning of Integer Programming Constraints | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=-3qCWheZhxU\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about CombOptNet:\n\n## Overview\n\nCombOptNet aims to integrate integer programming solvers into neural network architectures as layers capable of learning both the cost terms and the constraints, resulting in end-to-end trainable architectures that jointly extract features from raw data and solve a suitable (learned) combinatorial problem with state-of-the-art integer programming solvers.\n\n## Key Concept\n\nThe work addresses the fundamental challenge of bridging logical and algorithmic reasoning with modern machine learning, recognizing that many NP-Hard problems can be expressed as integer programs, in which the constraints play the role of their \"combinatorial specification\".\n\n## Applications and Results\n\nThe paper demonstrates the potential of such layers with an extensive performance analysis on synthetic data and with a demonstration on a competitive computer vision keypoint matching benchmark. The approach is tested on problems including MAX-CUT, KNAPSACK, and TRAVELLING SALESMAN problems.\n\n## Repository\n\nThe repository contains a PyTorch implementation of the paper. You can find the code and resources at the official GitHub repository (martius-lab/CombOptNet).\n\nThe paper was published in 2021 and represents an important contribution to combining deep learning with classical combinatorial optimization techniques.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e431d1d7-3cd3-4e4b-b594-f2d340c0cf89","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:34.448Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e7c10bab-6210-4b22-b713-2b605d174e20","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b9d72e84-d666-4818-a800-abd2efe26dfb","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a3dd1dc86014a90af","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DPKbhbGEb9cvB1Li8PngzJ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT hint warm start solution OR-Tools machine learning initial solution 2024\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT, UNKNOWN status with complete solution hint · Issue #3750 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3750\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT/Python how to provide an intial solution · Issue #1152 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1152\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT/Python how to save an initial solution and use it for next stage optimization · Issue #1542 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1542\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"📈 #76 Optimizing with Google OR-Tools: strategies and insights from three years of real-world experience\",\"url\":\"https://www.feasible.club/p/76-optimizing-with-google-or-tools\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"}]\n\nI've performed the web search on CP-SAT hints, warm start solutions, and OR-Tools. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Solution Hints as Warm Starts\n\nYou can inform CP-SAT to incorporate knowledge into its search through hints, and some workers will try to follow these hints, which can significantly improve solver performance if they are good. If the hints actually represent a feasible solution, the solver can use them to prune the search space of all branches that have worse bounds than the hints.\n\n## How to Add Hints in CP-SAT\n\nThe `add_hint()` method adds 'var == value' as a hint to the solver, appending the variable index and hinted value to the model's solution hint.\n\n## Important Limitations\n\nHints must cover all variables they touch and remain feasible after presolve or they're ignored silently, and if the solver finds no feasible solutions, your hint was inconsistent. Additionally, if solver stops by time limit in presolve, CP-SAT can't provide solution from hints.\n\n## Recent Updates\n\nThe last release 9.12 in February added Python 3.13 support, revamped hint handling, and sped up the linear expression layer. CP-SAT swept all gold medals in the 2024 MiniZinc Challenge and did almost the same the year before.\n\nThe search results focus on traditional constraint programming approaches rather than specific machine learning-based initial solution generation techniques for CP-SAT.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5d6eca89-ee17-427a-9cc2-b98113b10c89","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:36.617Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b9d72e84-d666-4818-a800-abd2efe26dfb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
