{"parentUuid":"40afa810-413e-420e-9c30-7fc3afc22c46","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a3dd1dc86014a90af","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Fo4nacpJkVJjm5tJUA8rNJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BRpuzmsDh1vcLyLixz8vUU","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"GNN training samples required imitation strong branching MILP 10000 instances generalization"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4340,"cache_read_input_tokens":32598,"output_tokens":131,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4340},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":131,"cache_read_input_tokens":32598,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4340,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4340,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caop1NtoRoymQG9ztV6un","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"817fab02-e8f5-4c49-b0dd-dbbbfb457965","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:53.504Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"817fab02-e8f5-4c49-b0dd-dbbbfb457965","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a3dd1dc86014a90af","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BRpuzmsDh1vcLyLixz8vUU","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"GNN training samples required imitation strong branching MILP 10000 instances generalization\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"SORREL: Suboptimal-Demonstration-Guided Reinforcement Learning for Learning to Branch\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2412.15534\"},{\"title\":\"SORREL: Suboptimal-Demonstration-Guided\",\"url\":\"https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/AAAI/article/download/33219/35374\"},{\"title\":\"A Deep Instance Generative Framework for MILP Solvers ...\",\"url\":\"https://papers.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2023/file/5297e56ac65ba2bfa70ee9fc4818c042-Paper-Conference.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Published in Transactions on Machine Learning Research (09/2022)\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=EQpGkw5rvL\"},{\"title\":\"Hybrid Models for Learning to Branch Prateek Gupta∗ University of Oxford\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2006.15212\"},{\"title\":\"MIP-GNN: A Data-Driven Framework for Guiding Combinatorial Solvers | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/361741429_MIP-GNN_A_Data-Driven_Framework_for_Guiding_Combinatorial_Solvers\"},{\"title\":\"A Deep Instance Generative Framework for MILP Solvers Under Limited Data Availability\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2310.02807\"},{\"title\":\"Data-Driven Optimization: Enhancing Combinatorial Optimization Solvers with Machine Learning | Analytics Magazine\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/do/10.1287/LYTX.2023.04.11/full/\"},{\"title\":\"Branching Strategies Based on Subgraph GNNs: A Study on Theoretical Promise versus Practical Reality\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2512.09355\"},{\"title\":\"Rethinking the Capacity of Graph Neural Networks for Branching Strategy\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2402.07099\"}]\n\nThe web search results provide substantial information about GNN training for learning branching strategies in MILP solving through imitation learning. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Training Dataset Size\n\n10,000 MILP instances are used for training, 2,000 instances for validation, and 100 instances for testing in several recent works following the experimental protocol established by foundational research in this area.\n\n## Imitation Learning with Strong Branching\n\nGraph Neural Networks are trained to predict promising variables for branching in Branch & Bound by imitating strong branching decisions on a bipartite graph representation of MILPs. The effectiveness of models trained via imitation learning relies on the availability of high-quality training data generated by near-optimal branching strategies such as the full strong branching strategy.\n\n## Generalization\n\nTesting instances from a transfer distribution are used to evaluate the generalization performance of these models. The approach performs well even on larger graphs than those used for training, indicating good out-of-distribution generalization capabilities.\n\n## Data Efficiency Challenges\n\nThe limited availability of real-world instances, due to labor-intensive data collection and proprietary issues, remains a critical challenge to the research community. This has motivated recent work on generative models to augment training datasets artificially.\n\nThe research indicates that while 10,000 instances is a standard benchmark size, there is ongoing investigation into data efficiency and generalization across different MILP problem classes.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"765cc936-e91a-4832-92bd-38f18d1f7109","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:07:00.963Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"817fab02-e8f5-4c49-b0dd-dbbbfb457965","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"765cc936-e91a-4832-92bd-38f18d1f7109","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a3dd1dc86014a90af","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_013YdUkbkWiSbq2MV79RgCLh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have sufficient research. Here is the consolidated assessment.\n\n---\n\n# GNN 与 Learning-to-Branch 在 70×70 设施放置上的可行性调研\n\n## 1. NeuroSAT 路线（Selsam 2018 → G4SATBench 2024）\n\nNeuroSAT 是开山之作，但**只能 scale 到几千变量**。后续 NeuroCore、NeuroBack（ICLR 2024）把 GNN 退回到\"给 CDCL 做 phase/branching 提示\"的辅助角色。G4SATBench (TMLR 2024) 系统性 benchmark 显示：纯 GNN 端到端解 SAT 在大规模仍不可行，**只有作为 hint/ranker 时有几个百分点的稳定收益**。我们 70×70 的 binary 决策变量量级在 1e4–1e5，正好踩在 NeuroSAT 的 scaling 边界外。**适用性低**：直接端到端没戏，但作为 phase hint 思路可借鉴。\n\n## 2. Gasse et al. 2019 GCN Branching + Ecole（最成熟 baseline）\n\n[Gasse 2019 NeurIPS](https://arxiv.org/abs/1906.01629) 用 bipartite GCN 模仿 strong branching，[Ecole](https://github.com/ds4dm/ecole) 是配套的 SCIP-based 训练环境。标准 protocol：**10000 训练 + 2000 验证 + 100 测试 实例**，每个候选分支记录 SB 评分。在 set cover / facility location 上比 SCIP 默认快 1.5–3×。**关键问题**：\n- 接的是 SCIP/MILP，**不是 CP-SAT**——CP-SAT 内部走的是 SAT-style 决策 + LP 松弛 + 多策略 portfolio，没有干净的\"per-node branching callback\"接口让 GNN 介入。\n- 我们一次 candidate 跑 4–30 分钟，10000 实例 = 700–5000 GPU 小时只是采数据，远超我们能承受的训练成本。\n\n**适用性中**：思想可用（学习候选 ranking），但接到 CP-SAT 的工程代价巨大，倒不如继续 LightGBM ranker。\n\n## 3. DeepMind Neural Diving + Neural Branching（2020-2021）\n\n[Nair et al. 2021](https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.13349) 是规模最大的工程实证：在 1e3–1e6 变量的 Google 生产 MIP 上把 SCIP 提升 2–10×（个别数据集 1e5×）。**Neural Diving 这一路对我们最有借鉴价值**：GNN 预测部分变量赋值 → 锁定后让求解器解剩余子问题。我们的\"266 个强制设施\"恰好可以让 GNN 先猜测 50–100 个大块设施（5×5、6×4）的位置区域，CP-SAT 求解收缩后的子问题。**但**需要训练数据和迁移，问题分布要稳定。**适用性高，但启动成本最重**。\n\n## 4. AlphaChip / Mirhoseini Nature 2021 — 谨慎！\n\n[Mirhoseini et al. Nature 2021](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-021-03544-w) 用 edge-based GCN + RL 做芯片宏单元 placement，表面上和我们的问题最像。**但已陷入严重再现性争议**：[Cheng et al. arxiv 2306.09633](https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.09633) 用同一基准复现失败；Nature 2023 撤回了配套 commentary；2024 Markov 在 CACM 列出 16 项方法学疑点；ACM 给原文加了 Expression of Concern。**这条路工程量极大、训练数据要求 RL 自博弈、社区共识是结果存疑**。我们的问题有硬性形状/端口约束（chip placement 是软目标加权和），生搬硬套会失去 exact 性。**不推荐**。\n\n## 5. CombOptNet / 端到端 IP 学习（martius-lab）\n\n[CombOptNet ICML 2021](https://arxiv.org/abs/2105.02343) 把 IP 求解器做成可微 layer，但**只在 MAX-CUT/Knapsack/TSP 等小规模 toy 上验证**，规模和约束复杂度都和我们差几个量级。**没有现成预训练大模型可下载 finetune**——这是关键事实，目前不存在像 NLP 里 BERT 那样可以拿来即用的\"通用 SAT/CSP GNN\"。**适用性低**。\n\n## 6. GFPack++ / 2D 不规则 packing 学习（2024）\n\n[GFPack++ arxiv 2406.07579](https://arxiv.org/html/2406.07579v1) 用 attention-based gradient field 学 2D 不规则 packing，纯 layout 视角。但它是**启发式**——不保证最优，没有端口/流约束建模能力，也无法证明 exact-bound。我们对 exactness 有硬要求（PROJECT_LOCK.md 规定），这条路只能在 exploratory 模式用。\n\n## 7. 图表征评估\n\n我们问题自然映射成 **bipartite graph**：facility 节点（266 个）+ grid cell 节点（4900 个）+ 端口连接边。规模适中、稀疏度高，结构上接近 facility location MIP，比 NeuroSAT 的纯 SAT 图友好得多。节点特征已经现成（设施类型、形状、电力、端口数）。**图本身可学，瓶颈在数据采集和把推理塞进 CP-SAT 而不引入 per-node latency**。\n\n## 8. 数据需求与现实\n\n- 标准 protocol：10000 训练实例，每个采 SB 评分轨迹。\n- 我们一个 candidate 4–30 分钟 → **10000 × 平均 10 分钟 = 1700 GPU·h**，光采数据要烧两个月单机。\n- Self-play / curriculum：60×60 → 70×70 → 80×80 的迁移在 [Toenshoff 2020](https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.08387) 和 Nair 2021 上都验证过 10× scaling 内可行，但**前提是分布稳定**——我们改 recipe 就破坏分布。\n\n## 推荐：2 个最值 PoC 的方向\n\n**A. Neural Diving 简化版（首推，3-4 周 PoC）**: 训一个 bipartite GNN，输入当前 candidate 的 facility 集合 + 部分已求解 instance 的轨迹，输出 50 个最大设施（5×5/6×4/3×3）的\"高置信度初始坐标\"。这些坐标作为 **CP-SAT `add_hint()`**（我们已有这个机制）喂入。**完全 shadow-only**，符合 AI Safety Contract，对错也只是 hint 失效。数据可以从 S0–S6 已跑过的几千个 candidate trace 中蒸馏，不需要新跑万级实例。\n\n**B. GNN Candidate Ranker（升级 LightGBM，2 周 PoC）**: 用 bipartite GCN（Gasse 风格）替换当前 LightGBM ranker，仅做 **outer candidate 排序**，**不进 CP-SAT 内部**——避开 per-node 推理延迟和接口对接。比较和 LightGBM 的 NDCG@10。如果提升 < 5%，放弃；提升明显则推到 S7+ 阶段。\n\n**避坑**：不要碰 AlphaChip 路线（社区共识有问题）、不要追 NeuroSAT 端到端（scaling 不够）、不要试 CombOptNet（无生产案例）。\n\n## 关键参考链接\n\n- [Gasse 2019 GCN branching](https://arxiv.org/abs/1906.01629) + [Ecole](https://github.com/ds4dm/ecole)\n- [Nair 2021 Neural Diving + Branching (DeepMind)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.13349)\n- [G4SATBench TMLR 2024](https://github.com/zhaoyu-li/G4SATBench)\n- [SORREL AAAI 2025 sample-efficient L2B](https://arxiv.org/html/2412.15534)\n- [Awesome ML4CO 资源整合](https://github.com/Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co)\n- [CP-SAT Primer (add_hint 用法)](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/)\n- [Toenshoff 2020 GNN for Max-CSP](https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.08387)\n- [AlphaChip 争议背景 (CACM)](https://cacm.acm.org/research/reevaluating-googles-reinforcement-learning-for-ic-macro-placement/)\n- [GFPack++ 2D packing](https://arxiv.org/html/2406.07579v1)\n- [CombOptNet](https://github.com/martius-lab/CombOptNet)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1385,"cache_read_input_tokens":36938,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1385,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caop2Dy49KRrFXfsaS17D","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"98b0dba3-4bbb-489a-bf86-7aa28716a418","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:08:02.653Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
